# intro1 — the redislings ritual
#
# Most exercises are a file of commands, one per line, that redislings pipes
# into redis-cli (or valkey-cli) against a brand-new, empty server:
#
#     grep -v '^#' commands.redis | redis-cli -p 6390
#
# Lines starting with # are comments; redislings strips them first because
# redis-cli itself has no comment syntax. The check then looks at the data
# your commands left behind, or at what they printed. Once it passes, the
# exercise is done and redislings moves you on.
#
# To try things by hand, run `redislings server` in another terminal and
# connect with `redis-cli -p 6390` (or `valkey-cli -p 6390`). That server
# forgets everything when you stop it.
#
# Task: the check wants the key `greeting` to hold "hello, redis". Fix the
# SET below and save.

SET greeting "hello, world"
GET greeting
